#: 01.md:1
msgid "Tutorial 1:<br>Determining a scattering profile with hySAS"
msgstr "Tutorial 1：<br>hySAS による Scattering Profile の決定"

#: 01.md:3
msgid ""
"In the next example, we calculate the scattering profile of a structure "
"consisting of atoms 1-11558 using the ONEBEAD approach. This structure could"
" be made of protein(s), DNA, RNA, or complexes. As a first step, let's "
"create and open the `plumed.dat` file, which will contain all the "
"instructions:"
msgstr ""
"次の例では、原子1〜11558の構造の Scattering Profile を ONEBEAD "
"で計算します。タンパク質、DNA、RNA、複合体のいずれでもかまいません。まず全指示を入れる `plumed.dat` を作って開きます。"

#: 01.md:8
msgid ""
"The first requirement is to provide the PDB of the structure via MOLINFO, in"
" this case `template_AA.pdb`. Detailed information about the input file can "
"be found in the technical support section."
msgstr ""
"MOLINFO に構造の PDB、ここでは `template_AA.pdb` を指定します。入力の詳細は Technical Support "
"を参照してください。"

#: 01.md:12
msgid ""
"The SAS instructions need the corresponding action option, which can be "
"either SAXS or SANS. In the following example, we proceed by opening the "
"SAXS action:"
msgstr "SAS には SAXS または SANS の Action が必要です。ここでは SAXS を開きます。"

#: 01.md:18
msgid ""
"The SAXS calculation options must be listed with the appropriate flags, in "
"any order. Here, we include atoms 1-11878 and specify the ONEBEAD mapping (1"
" bead for 1 amino acid, 3 beads for 1 nucleotide). The same "
"`template_AA.pdb` is used for both MOLINFO and TEMPLATE. The GPU flag allows"
" the calculation of the scattering profile(s) on the GPU; this feature "
"requires PLUMED to be compiled with support for the ArrayFire library. See "
"the corresponding technical support section in this manual for more "
"information. The electron density of the solvent is set to 0.334 electrons "
"per cubic angstrom (bulk water) with the SOLVDENS flag. In the example, the "
"solvation layer contribution is ignored by setting "
"SOLVATION_CORRECTION=0.00. For this reason, other flags such as SASA_CUTOFF "
"and SOLVATION_STRIDE are not required. Further examples are given at the end"
" of this page."
msgstr ""
"SAXS のオプションは任意の順で Flag を並べます。原子1〜11878を含め、ONEBEAD（1アミノ酸に1 Bead、1 Nucleotide "
"に3 Bead）を指定します。MOLINFO と TEMPLATE は同じ `template_AA.pdb` です。GPU Flag は GPU "
"計算を有効にし、ArrayFire 対応でビルドした PLUMED が必要です。詳細は Technical Support "
"を参照してください。SOLVDENS は Bulk Water の電子密度0.334 "
"electrons/Å³です。SOLVATION_CORRECTION=0.00 で Solvation Layer "
"を無視するため、SASA_CUTOFF や SOLVATION_STRIDE は不要です。ページ末尾にも例があります。"

#: 01.md:32
msgid ""
"After the option flags, the user has to provide the list of q-values for "
"which the corresponding SAS intensity must be calculated. In this example, "
"we provide 121 q-values, from almost zero to 0.3 Å<sup>-1</sup> (which "
"corresponds to the maximum momentum transfer available for the ONEBEAD "
"mapping), every 0.0025 Å<sup>-1</sup>. The more the q-values, the more "
"intensive the calculation. After listing the q-values, the SAXS action must "
"be closed and the intensities printed. In the case of a trajectory, it is "
"possible to select the printing frequency. In the example, the intensities "
"are printed at every simulation step, specifying STRIDE=1. Additional `{}` "
"brackets have been added to prevent a readability issue, they are optional "
"to run the code. Save and close the file."
msgstr ""
"次に SAS Intensity を計算する q 値を列挙します。ここではほぼ0から ONEBEAD の最大 Momentum Transfer 0.3"
" Å<sup>-1</sup> まで、0.0025 Å<sup>-1</sup> 刻みの121点です。点が多いほど計算量が増えます。その後 SAXS "
"を閉じ、Intensity を出力します。Trajectory の出力頻度も選べ、ここでは STRIDE=1 で全 Step に出します。追加の "
"`{}` は表示の読みやすさのためで、実行には任意です。保存して閉じます。"

#: 01.md:172
msgid ""
"As an additional example, we provide a SANS action with a different setup. "
"The solvent layer contribution is set to 80 electrons/nm<sup>3</sup>. Since "
"we want to calculate the SANS intensity, there will be an automatic "
"conversion from electron density to water molecule density. Unlike the "
"previous example, the solvation correction is now activated. We specified "
"the solvent exposed area threshold for a bead to 1 nm<sup>2</sup> using the "
"flag SASA_CUTOFF. The bead exposure is evaluated by the LCPO algorithm, and "
"since calculating it for each step of the simulation could be "
"computationally expensive, it is possible to set the frequency for the "
"solvent-accessible surface area estimation with the SOLVATION_STRIDE flag. "
"By default, it is set to 10 steps. Finally, the fraction of deuterated "
"solvent is specified with DEUTER_CONC. This information is also used to "
"configure the implicit hydrogen-deuterium exchange: with a probability equal"
" to the deuterium concentration in the solvent (60% in this case), an "
"exposed bead is considered deuterated."
msgstr ""
"別設定の SANS の例も示します。Solvent Layer の寄与は80 electrons/nm<sup>3</sup> で、SANS "
"では電子密度から水分子密度に自動変換します。今回は Solvation 補正を有効にし、SASA_CUTOFF で露出判定の閾値を1 "
"nm<sup>2</sup> とします。LCPO による露出判定は高コストなので、SOLVATION_STRIDE で SASA "
"計算間隔を設定でき、既定は10 Step です。DEUTER_CONC は Deuterated Solvent の割合です。同じ情報を暗黙的な "
"Hydrogen-Deuterium Exchange に使い、溶媒中の Deuterium 濃度（ここでは60%）と等しい確率で、露出 Bead を "
"Deuterated とみなします。"

